   "txt": "**1. Single Most Important Fact**\nL&T Energy Hydrocarbon Offshore (LTEH Offshore) has secured an **\"Ultra-Mega\" EPCIC order valued at over \u20b915,000 crore** for a strategic offshore development project from a client in the Middle East.\n\n---\n\n**2. Key Numbers Exactly as Stated**\n* **Order Value:** Classified as **Ultra-Mega (> \u20b915,000 Crore)** as per L&T's order classification threshold (exact contract value not separately specified).\n* *(No revenue, EBITDA, or PAT numbers are applicable or stated in this contract announcement filing).*\n\n---\n\n**3. Management Guidance & Forward Statements**\n* **T Madhava Das (Whole-time Director, Senior EVP & Head - Energy Hydrocarbon Division):** Stated that this is *\"one of the most significant offshore developments currently underway in the Middle East and underscores the growing investments being made to meet future energy demand,\"* requiring deep engineering expertise and flawless coordination.\n* **Parthasarathi Chatterjee (Senior VP & Head \u2013 LTEH Offshore):** Highlighted that the project involves multiple offshore facilities, subsea infrastructure, and substantial fabrication, executed via an integrated EPCIC approach.\n* **Execution details:** A significant portion of fabrication activities will take place at L&T's integrated manufacturing and fabrication facilities.\n\n---\n\n**4. What a Shareholder Should Watch or Act On**\n* **Order Book & Execution:** Adds substantial revenue visibility (>\u20b915,000 Cr) to the hydrocarbon vertical; track execution milestones, supply chain/marine asset deployment, and margin realization on large-scale Middle East projects.\n\n---\n\n**5. One-Line Net Read**\n* **Positive:** A massive order win (>\u20b915,000 Cr) reinforces L&T's international order inflow momentum and strong execution presence in the Middle East offshore hydrocarbon market."
